# Beneath (PPSA27640) -- boot to gameplay: Science_Remake2, the opening dive.
#
# VALIDATED on Linux with hardware Vulkan (RADV, AMD Radeon 8060S / STRIX_HALO), native
# 1920x1080, headless `tools/screenshot` frontend, PROSPER_RENDER=1, no render acceleration.
#
# THIS TITLE NEEDS PROSPER_NULL_PAGE=1 TO BOOT AT ALL. Without it the guest's primary thread dies
# 1.1 s in with SIGSEGV at addr=0x8, rip=eboot+0xe44346 -- a frame-pointer-chain unwinder reading
# the return-address slot of a NULL frame pointer. See docs/BENEATH_STATUS.md; the underlying
# defect is tracked separately. Every window below is measured with that variable set.
#
# WHAT THE ROUTE HAS TO GET PAST, in the title's own words (strings from
# Media/sharedassets4.assets, the localisation table):
#
#   title screen   " Press Any Button To Start "   (_Start)
#   main menu      NEW GAME / LOAD GAME / OPTIONS / CREDITS / EXIT, NEW GAME preselected
#   GAME MODE      SELECT DIFFICULTY -- TOURIST PASS / COLD REALITY / HARD BASTARD,
#                  TOURIST PASS preselected (it renders in green in the capture)
#   INTRO          Assets/LEVELS/INTRO/Intro.unity, a narration sequence
#
# Every one of those four gates is answered by CROSS, and CROSS is preselected on both lists, so
# the opening ladder is Cross-only and self-synchronising: surplus presses simply wait on whatever
# screen the boot happens to be on. Route timing is effectively wall-clock (#2764) -- the guest
# polls the pad from early boot, not from the first interactive screen -- so the ladder is
# deliberately long rather than tightly anchored.
#
# CROSS IS MEASURED HARMLESS IN-GAME for this title: the exploratory arm mashed it from t=87 s
# (level14 open) to t=360 s without leaving the scene, changing scene, or faulting. That is what
# lets the ladder run long enough to cover a slow boot.
#
# NO CROSS AFTER t=240. The stick windows below are movement in-game, but they are LIST NAVIGATION
# on the main menu, and `up` on a preselected top entry can wrap onto EXIT. Ending the ladder
# before the sticks start means a slow boot can still land a selection on EXIT but can never
# CONFIRM it -- the route has no button left that would commit it.
#
# PROGRESS ORACLE IS THE UNITY SCENE INDEX, NOT PIXELS. Media/levelNN is the build-settings scene
# index: Media/globalgamemanagers holds exactly 46 scene paths at contiguous offsets
# 218784..221088, and Media/ holds exactly 46 levelNN files (level0..level45). 46 == 46,
# index-for-index. Self-check: of the 12 levelNN files that carry a .resS streamed-resource
# sidecar below level5, every one lands on a world scene (14,15,16,20,24,25,26,27,30,31,39,44)
# and not one lands on a loading screen, so a mis-derived index would break that partition rather
# than yield a plausible wrong answer.
#
#   level0  Preload            level4  Menu/MenuD (main menu)     level7  LOADING_SCREENS/LoadShip
#   level1  Menu/Health_W      level5  INTRO/Intro                level14 SCIENCE_SHIP/Science_Remake2
#   level2  Menu/ShaderPreload level6  LOADING_SCREENS/backMainMenu
#   level3  Menu/Launcher
#
# GAMEPLAY DISCRIMINATOR: any world scene, i.e. levelN for N in
# {14,15,16,18,20,24,25,26,27,28,30,31,34,39,42,44}. A new game loads level14 first, and level7
# (LoadShip) is the loading screen that immediately precedes it.
#
# Measured on the validated run (PROSPER_FILELOG=1 open lines, timestamped against
# PROSPER_PAD_SCRIPT_LOG elapsed=):
#
#   t~0     level0 + level1     preload
#   t~6.5   level2 + level3     shader preload, launcher
#   t~18    level4              main menu
#   t~48.5  level5              INTRO
#   t~84.5  level7              LoadShip
#   t~87    level14             Science_Remake2 -- GAMEPLAY
#
# A second, independent content check that does not reuse the scene derivation: the waypoint HUD
# marker ("39m", the _WaypointO / WAYPOINT DISTANCE readout) is drawn only in-world, and it is
# visible in every gameplay sample.

# --- phase 1: the opening ladder -- title screen, NEW GAME, GAME MODE, INTRO.
